<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aung San</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1915–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bogyoke Aung San</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aung San was a Burmese nationalist leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma-independence-army">Burma Independence Army</a> with Japanese help in 1941. He led the army of the Japanese-sponsored State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> but turned it against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1945. He negotiated independence with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and agreed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panglong-conference">Panglong Conference</a> with Shan, Kachin and Chin leaders in 1947, but was assassinated in July 1947, months before independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aung-san.jpg" alt="Aung San" width="300" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aung_San_color_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
